  "method": "HeroLab (src/Core/HeroLab.cs, AimForge --hero-lab all): the PsyLab human model and shipping curve math on five kit-derived fights per hero; projectile lead, recoil pull-down, descending aim, ballistic minimum-jerk switches with tempo variability and one corrective submovement; relative scoring per fight; snap x Y/X x game filter; robustness across five hand models. The selection rule is identical for every hero.",
  "modelCorrectionsDuringTheWork": [
    "v1 raw worst-case + narrow 3% pool picked a curve with 76% re-acquire spread for Loki - consistency was invisible inside the sim",
    "v2 added throw-tempo variability to switches (hand plan learned at nominal tempo, executed at +-14%)",
    "v3 added the kit's big re-acquire turn to every hero; v4 made switches two-component (ballistic throw, one corrective submovement)",
    "v5 relative scoring per fight (raw worst-case let the hardest fight pick every card)",
    "v6 switches as minimum-jerk throws at realistic tempo (the 2.5 Hz tracking follower made 90-degree flicks take ~350 ms and sit inside every ramp) - the shipped cards"
